    !! wrong method of repair
        - too encumbered with premature rhetoric, what follows
        - leads me astray and into confusion
    - … entry to practical philosophy … the cosmic safehold,
      … key … the question, ‘To what end?’
\ to warrant these claims and this metaphor, their explication:
    - hardly could … contemplate the prospect of entering the safehold without asking that question,
      nor make headway in the philosophy without … an answer [in the context of the safehold]
\ to warrant these claims re (cQ) the question and (cA) its answer, the following:
\ to warrant (cQ), one of:
    | {[emphasis of] the fact|phenomenon of [impulsive] force and tension, of it being hard to resist
      both (i) reaching for the safehold and (ii) asking in regard to (i) the question}
        : see notepad:2026-9-14a,b
    | [the scale|scope of] the safehold makes remote and obscure the ultimate end,
      which in turn presses|urges the question, making it a must-ask as claimed
\ to warrant (cA):
    | working (in response to the impulse) to answer the question reveals that [the fact|phenomenon
      of] the impulse is [to be] *expected* as part of a moral obligation
            \ so warranting the claim of headway, and specifically headway into practical philosophy
        : see notepad:2026-9-14c
\ to warrant the above claim, one of:
    | {entering straight into the argument}
        : viz. `^*\+ enter into the philosophy by stating the full argument to complete the text$` @
          ../02.wrong_rhetoric/._/wrong_rhetoric.README_boneyard.brec
    | {explicating further in summary}
        |
            - urgently desiring that together we reach for it, at first I simply assumed
              that our carrying on would suffice as an answer, and sought direct proof
              of a moral obligation to that end
                : cf. `^*\| working.+in response to the impulse.+ to answer the question` : There I
                  recall working in response to implulse (ii).  Here I recall earlier satisfying (ii)
                  with an assumption and working more directly in response to implulse (i).
                    : re    `implulse (\(i\))`    see `${same} reaching for the safehold`
                    : re `(?:implulse )?(\(ii\))` see `${same} asking in regard to \(i\) the question`
            \ so setting up for:
            : see notepad:2026-9-15a,b : ‘My intuitive default-morals insight
              will get me to the need of a ground in “To what end?” … ’
                : re `the need of a (ground)`
                  viz. `what is crucial herein, that.+a ${same} is being sought`s
